Package: powerbi-linux
Version: 0.1.0-19~experimental1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Power BI Linux <cavallaro88@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/cavallaro88/powerbi-linux
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12), systemd (>= 250), winbind, desktop-file-utils, shared-mime-info, hicolor-icon-theme, xdg-utils, zenity, cabextract, fontconfig, libfreetype6, libvulkan1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbregistry0, libgnutls30t64, libunwind8, libegl1, libodbc2, libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, libpulse0, libasound2t64, libpcap0.8t64, libgstreamer1.0-0, libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-0
Description: experimental Power BI Desktop compatibility tools for Linux
 CLI installer, launcher and desktop integration for a community Wine runtime.
 Ubuntu 24.04/26.04 and Debian 13 on x86_64 with Wayland are experimental:
 compatibility is not certified. A systemd user session and a suitable
 Vulkan driver are required. Fedora 44 remains the tested target.
 Beta candidate: the package version, setup metadata and packaging behavior may
 change; no stable release is certified.
 Microsoft Power BI Desktop, .NET, WebView2 and the Wine runtime are
 obtained separately per user. This package contains no Microsoft software
 or Wine prefix. Resource settings remain user-controlled; packaging does
 not apply a preset.
